This project investigates the application of neural networks to develop a personalized music recommendation system for Spotify. The study utilizes a dataset of song attributes—such as danceability, energy, and genre—alongside user interaction logs to train and evaluate four distinct predictive models: Content-Based, Collaborative Filtering, Neural Collaborative Filtering, and a Hybrid model. The Hybrid approach, which integrates collaborative user/product embeddings, content-based audio features, and contextual data, achieved the best overall performance and stability, effectively mitigating traditional limitations like the cold-start problem. While the advanced neural network architectures demonstrated a strong ability to capture complex non-linear interactions, the researchers noted that high computational training costs and data scarcity for new entities remain challenges for future development.
